% oracle: colour
% Scenario: a gray space that does not collapse. A CIEBasedA space whose
% MatrixA is half the white point rather than the white point itself is
% carried as Lab; 0.5 through the gamma of 2 is a quarter, so the first
% fill is a neutral grey at an eighth of the white point's luminance,
% and 0.9 gives one at 0.405 of it.
[/CIEBasedA <<
  /WhitePoint [0.9505 1 1.089]
  /DecodeA {2 exp} bind
  /MatrixA [0.47525 0.5 0.5445]
>>] setcolorspace
0.5 setcolor
100 100 200 100 rectfill
0.9 setcolor
100 300 200 100 rectfill
showpage
